  "implementation": [
    "ChatActivityTimeline ports the web boundary and observation-order rules; missing or conflicting positions retain legacy layout.",
    "MessageProseView gives each stable text span its own WebView height and fallback state while reader/copy actions retain full-response scope.",
    "AppModel owns per-block summary choices separately from the existing default-on AppStorage preference; explicit global changes reset local choices.",
    "Inline tools retain status, source, failure visibility, existing lazy output reads and per-tool expansion; semantic status changes use UIKit announcements.",
    "Disclosure touch targets are at least 44 points and summary titles wrap at accessibility text sizes."
  ],
  "verified": [
    "17 shared TypeScript/Swift scenarios cover Unicode, markup/code boundaries, image decks, same-name tools, retained attempts, legacy fallback and invalid chronology.",
    "133 selected native unit tests and 12 Activity UI tests pass, including prior runtime identity, legacy tools and output-scope refusal cases.",
    "Native rendered order is summary, prose, tool, summary, prose. Local summary/tool choices survive background/foreground and completion; a newly arriving block respects opt-out.",
    "Failures remain visible under opt-out; global hide/show resets local choices; completed tool output opens and dismisses through the existing sheet.",
    "Largest accessibility text renders the whole summary title and tool label within the viewport. Screenshots are automated simulator evidence, not human VoiceOver acceptance.",
    "Release warm-journey smoke passes. Its test duration is not a quantitative performance measurement."
  ],
  "retainedFailuresAndCorrections": [
    "The first shared-fixture run used an invalid failed phase; corrected the fixture to the established error phase.",
    "The initial UI locators assumed child identifiers and one accessibility node per WebView. The observed hierarchy supplies the parent identifier and nested WebView nodes; tests now scope those actual nodes.",
    "The global-toggle test tapped the label area, which did not move the native switch. Targeting the observed trailing thumb verifies persistence and reset semantics.",
    "A green large-text test still showed a truncated title. The title now wraps; the check compares text height to native font metrics and positions the full tool below the sticky date header.",
    "The first Release check was explicitly interrupted (exit 75) when screenshot review showed remaining large-text crowding. The header now uses explicit top alignment and vertical spacing, with title bounds checked against the preceding tool.",
    "The first wrapping assertion incorrectly required an 80-point header despite a fully rendered 74.67-point header; replaced that arbitrary threshold with font-relative multiline evidence.",
    "An attempted tsx invocation failed because the repo does not install tsx; the existing Node strip-types/alias-loader command passed."
  ],
